I have been following this issue for a while without being fully sure that it's related to some problems I've observed [in another project](https://gitlab.com/CalyxOS/calyxos/-/issues/2642#note_2218874787), related to CameraX. I haven't wanted to share something unrelated or unhelpful here, so apologies if that's the case or if this is duplicative info, but the issue is quite long. At this stage, though, after continuing to see so many comments, I want to to share what I've noticed in case it _is_ useful and someone who is reading this has more luck / time to try some things, or can point me in the right direction.

As I wrote elsewhere:
> CameraController listens to rotation changes, but it doesn't check what the current rotation is before that, and never sets target rotations *except* when the rotation *changes*. This seems like it *may* be a bug, but I'm not sure. It would explain why the orientation is off when switching cameras, unless you go out of your way to rotate a particular way and back.
